WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.835
-Good evening, I'm Seth Meyers
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:05.204
We hope you're doing well,
and let's get to the news.

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:08.675
President Biden received his
coronavirus vaccine booster shot

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:13.613
yesterday, or as Fox News
reported, heroin.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:16.983
While receiving his coronavirus
vaccine booster shot yesterday,

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:20.386
President Biden told reporters
"I know it doesn't look like it,

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.688
but I am over 65."

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:25.024
But I don't know what's worse,
how corny that joke is

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:29.262
or the fact that he's been using
it for 13 years.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.664
Senate Minority Leader
Mitch McConnell yesterday

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.099
also received a coronavirus
vaccine booster shot.

00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:36.769
McConnell received
a shot in his hand because,

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:39.572
of course,
he tried to block it.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:45.944
[ Vocalizes ]

00:00:45.944 --> 00:00:49.649
Defense Secretary Lloyd Austin
and joint chiefs of staff

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.685
Chairman General Mark Milley
appeared publicly today

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.355
before the Senate for the first
time since the U.S.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:57.957
withdrawal from Afghanistan,
and they immediately

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.825
had to be evacuated,
"Go, go, go!

00:00:59.825 --> 00:01:02.161
We didn't think
it'd be this bad!"

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.630
According to a new book by
ex-White House press secretary

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.866
Stephanie Grisham,
former President Trump

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.435
cuts his own hair with a huge
pair of scissors that would

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:13.072
"cut a ribbon at an opening of
one of his properties."

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:16.643
And now, two years later,
the bank owns his hair.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:19.045
After the adult film star
Stormy Daniels described

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.380
former President Trump's penis
in an interview,

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.683
Trump purportedly called then
White House staffer

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:26.819
Stephanie Grisham and assured he
that Daniels' description

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:29.755
was incorrect, I can't imagine
exactly what he said

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:33.259
but probably something like...
-I was in the pool!

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.461
I was in the pool!

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.196
-Something like that.

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:39.532
President Biden is reportedly
annoyed at the White House

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.400
press corps for asking off-topic
questions.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.602
As a string of recent meetings
with foreign leaders,

00:01:43.602 --> 00:01:48.875
besides, he has no idea why
Samantha's not coming back.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.677
The annual
Congressional Baseball Game

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:53.112
is set for tomorrow, pitting
Democrats against Republicans,

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:56.282
so hurry up and pick a team,
Joe.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:59.786
French President Emmanuel Macron
was hit by an egg yesterday

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:02.655
while touring an international
food trade fair.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:09.195
Said Macron, "That's ah-neuf."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:12.631
Karen Chee submitted that joke
and in her submission said to

00:02:12.631 --> 00:02:15.135
Alex Baze, "I believe that this
joke is perfect."

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.970
[ Laughter ]
Is that accurate, Baze?

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.607
So, do please, go to...

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:23.876
where you'll be
given the option of voting

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:27.447
"Yes, that was a perfect joke."
Or "Karen."

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.014
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.014 --> 00:02:32.151
And finally, C-Span recently
unveiled a new app called

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:36.422
C-Span now, also available on
most White Noise apps.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.590
And that was the Monologue.

